        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="logical-model-guide" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=20;" value="&lt;b&gt;Model documentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;p&gt;The remaining diagram pages specify conceptual mapping, nullability, value constraints and relationship guards. README.md contains the same rules in searchable text.&lt;/p&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="950" y="5010" width="2070" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="logical-notes-0" name="Mapping from the conceptual model">
    <mxGraphModel page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="2300" grid="1" gridSize="10">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="notes-content-0" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.45&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size:26px&quot;&gt;Mapping from the conceptual model&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Conceptual element&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Relational mapping&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;ACCOUNT, RESIDENT and VOLUNTEER&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each has its own table. &lt;code&gt;resident.account_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;volunteer.account_id&lt;/code&gt; are both primary keys and foreign keys to &lt;code&gt;account.account_id&lt;/code&gt;. An account may occur in both subtype tables and must occur in at least one (BR1). The account ID is the immutable username and Firebase UID. Email is held by Firebase (BR56).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Preferred postal codes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The multivalued volunteer attribute becomes &lt;code&gt;volunteer_preferred_postal_code(account_id, postal_code)&lt;/code&gt;. Its composite primary key prevents repeated codes for one volunteer (BR9).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Facility acceptance&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The many-to-many relationship between facilities and categories becomes &lt;code&gt;facility_accepts(facility_id, category_id)&lt;/code&gt;. Both columns form its primary key and reference their parent tables.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;STATUS_CHANGE&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;This weak entity uses &lt;code&gt;(pickup_request_id, changed_at)&lt;/code&gt; as its composite primary key. The request ID is also a foreign key. Every request starts with an Open history entry, and later entries are append-only (BR16–BR18).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request owner and category&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_request.account_id&lt;/code&gt; references &lt;code&gt;resident.account_id&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;category_id&lt;/code&gt; references &lt;code&gt;item_category.category_id&lt;/code&gt;. Each request has one owner and one category. The pickup address is copied at creation (BR13, BR34).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Pickup windows and assignments&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each window references its request. Each assignment references a request, volunteer, offered window and terms acceptance. The window and request must agree (BR19). Ended assignments and inactive windows remain as history.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Delivery&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;delivery.assignment_id&lt;/code&gt; references an assignment and is unique. Each delivery references one facility and one required evidence photo. This maps the assignment&amp;#x27;s optional one-to-one delivery relationship (BR25).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;EcoPoints recipient&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ecopoints_award&lt;/code&gt; references its assignment and either a resident or a volunteer. Exactly one recipient foreign key is populated (BR11). A self-delivery creates two award rows, one for each role.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Notifications&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each notification references one account and exactly one source, either a pickup request or an EcoPoints award (BR10, BR48).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Photos&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;photo.file_id&lt;/code&gt; is the ImageKit key. An optional request foreign key permits item photos to be reused by rescheduled requests. A delivery has one required evidence photo. A photo belongs to the request-photo relationship or the delivery-photo relationship (BR51, BR60).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Terms and push subscriptions&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Each acceptance references an account and a terms document. Each subscription references an account and is identified by its endpoint. Request and assignment acceptances must belong to their respective actors (BR29, BR43).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rescheduling&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The nullable self-reference &lt;code&gt;rescheduled_from_request_id&lt;/code&gt; links a new request to its missed predecessor. Its uniqueness allows each missed request to be rescheduled once (BR50).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Derived attributes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Request status comes from the latest status change. Assignment status comes from collection and ending fields. Delivery time comes from assignment ending time. Award kind and time come from its assignment. EcoPoints totals, expiry and eligible facilities are computed from their source relations (BR12, BR24, BR33, BR44–BR45, BR57, BR59).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="1400" height="2150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="logical-notes-1" name="Nullability">
    <mxGraphModel page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="2300" grid="1" gridSize="10">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="notes-content-1" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.45&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size:26px&quot;&gt;Nullability&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;All primary-key columns are required. Every column is &lt;code&gt;NOT NULL&lt;/code&gt; except the columns explicitly listed below. Composite foreign keys require all their columns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Relation&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Nullable columns and meaning&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;account&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;deactivated_at&lt;/code&gt; until deactivation.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;resident&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None. Street and Calgary postal code are required.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;volunteer&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;volunteer_preferred_postal_code&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None. Zero saved codes is represented by zero rows.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;push_subscription&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;expiration_time&lt;/code&gt; when the push service supplies no expiry, and &lt;code&gt;user_agent&lt;/code&gt; when unavailable.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;terms_document&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;terms_acceptance&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;item_category&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;photo&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None. Both the ImageKit file ID and path are required.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_request&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;notes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;file_id&lt;/code&gt; when there is no item photo, and &lt;code&gt;rescheduled_from_request_id&lt;/code&gt; for an original request.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_window&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;status_change&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;reason&lt;/code&gt; when no explanation was supplied.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;assignment&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;collected_at&lt;/code&gt; before collection, and &lt;code&gt;ended_at&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;end_reason&lt;/code&gt; until ending. Both ending fields must be null together or set together (BR23).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;delivery&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None. The assignment, facility and evidence &lt;code&gt;file_id&lt;/code&gt; are required.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;recycling_facility&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;special_instructions&lt;/code&gt; when absent.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;facility_accepts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;None.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ecopoints_award&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;resident_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;volunteer_id&lt;/code&gt;, with exactly one non-null.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;notification&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pushed_at&lt;/code&gt; until a push is actually sent, plus &lt;code&gt;pickup_request_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ecopoints_award_id&lt;/code&gt;, with exactly one source non-null. Metadata is a required JSON object, which may be empty.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="1400" height="2150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="logical-notes-2" name="Value constraints">
    <mxGraphModel page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="2300" grid="1" gridSize="10">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="notes-content-2" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.45&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size:26px&quot;&gt;Value constraints&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;account_id&lt;/code&gt; uses &lt;code&gt;VARCHAR(50)&lt;/code&gt; throughout. Account IDs are 3–50 lowercase characters from &lt;code&gt;a-z&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;0-9&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;-&lt;/code&gt; (contract Conventions). Required names and IDs must contain text.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Postal codes use &lt;code&gt;CHAR(6)&lt;/code&gt;, uppercase with no spaces, in Canadian letter-digit-letter-digit-letter-digit form. Calgary validity is checked during account/profile validation (BR7).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_request.quantity&lt;/code&gt; is an integer greater than zero. Category standard weight and request estimated weight are positive exact decimals. The stored request weight is calculated from quantity and the category weight when created or edited (BR30–BR31).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;pickup_window.start_hour&lt;/code&gt; is an integer from 0 through 23. A window stores its Calgary date and hour directly. The server validates future start times and the original creation-time limit, retaining inactive history (BR32–BR36).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;status_change.status&lt;/code&gt; is one of &lt;code&gt;Open&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Assigned&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Collected&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Delivered&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Expired&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Missed&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;reason&lt;/code&gt; is optional free text (BR17–BR18).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Non-null &lt;code&gt;assignment.end_reason&lt;/code&gt; is one of &lt;code&gt;Delivered&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Resident_Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Volunteer_Cancelled&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Missed_Pickup&lt;/code&gt;. Collection cannot precede acceptance, and ending cannot precede acceptance or collection. A Delivered assignment must have been collected (BR21–BR26).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;terms_acceptance.type&lt;/code&gt; is one of &lt;code&gt;AT_RESIDENT_REGISTRATION_OR_ACTIVATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_VOLUNTEER_REGISTRATION_OR_ACTIVATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_RESIDENT_REQUEST_CREATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AT_VOLUNTEER_ACCEPTANCE&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;notification.type&lt;/code&gt; uses the closed list from contract section 13.1, reproduced in the diagram&amp;#x27;s domain-rules panel. &lt;code&gt;is_read&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;is_expired&lt;/code&gt; and window &lt;code&gt;is_active&lt;/code&gt; are required booleans.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;EcoPoints use exact &lt;code&gt;NUMERIC(23,2)&lt;/code&gt; values and store the formula text used at award time. Volunteer points are &lt;code&gt;3 * quantity + 4 * estimated_weight_kg&lt;/code&gt;, and resident points are half the volunteer points, following BR41 and contract section 15.1.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="1400" height="2150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="logical-notes-3" name="Relationship and uniqueness constraints">
    <mxGraphModel page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1500" pageHeight="2300" grid="1" gridSize="10">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="notes-content-3" parent="1" vertex="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=20;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.45&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;font-size:26px&quot;&gt;Relationship and uniqueness constraints&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rule&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Logical constraint / enforcement&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Assignment uses a window from its own request (BR19)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;UNIQUE (pickup_request_id, pickup_window_id)&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;pickup_window&lt;/code&gt;, with composite foreign key &lt;code&gt;assignment(pickup_request_id, pickup_window_id)&lt;/code&gt; referencing that pair.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;One unfinished assignment per request (BR20)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Partial unique index on &lt;code&gt;assignment(pickup_request_id)&lt;/code&gt; where &lt;code&gt;ended_at IS NULL&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;One delivery per assignment (BR25)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;UNIQUE (assignment_id)&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;delivery&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A missed request is rescheduled once (BR50)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;UNIQUE (rescheduled_from_request_id)&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;pickup_request&lt;/code&gt;. The server also verifies that the referenced request was reported missed and prevents self-reference.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Exactly one award recipient (BR11)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;CHECK ((resident_id IS NOT NULL) &amp;lt;&amp;gt; (volunteer_id IS NOT NULL))&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;At most one award per assignment and role (BR55)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Separate partial unique indexes on &lt;code&gt;assignment_id&lt;/code&gt;, one where &lt;code&gt;resident_id IS NOT NULL&lt;/code&gt;, the other where &lt;code&gt;volunteer_id IS NOT NULL&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Exactly one notification source (BR48)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;CHECK ((pickup_request_id IS NOT NULL) &amp;lt;&amp;gt; (ecopoints_award_id IS NOT NULL))&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Ending fields agree (BR23)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;CHECK ((ended_at IS NULL) = (end_reason IS NULL))&lt;/code&gt;, together with the allowed end-reason values.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;No repeated preferred code or facility/category pair&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Composite primary keys on the two relationship tables.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;No repeated active pickup slot&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Partial unique index on &lt;code&gt;(pickup_request_id, pickup_date, start_hour)&lt;/code&gt; where &lt;code&gt;is_active = TRUE&lt;/code&gt;. Historical inactive rows are retained.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A delivery photo belongs to one delivery (BR60)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #aaa;padding:10px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;UNIQUE (file_id)&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;delivery&lt;/code&gt;. A transaction/trigger verifies that the photo is not also referenced by a pickup request. Multiple requests may share an item photo after rescheduling.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;p&gt;The following rules involve several rows or time-dependent decisions. Enforce them in transactions that lock the relevant account/request/assignment, or with equivalent concurrency-safe database triggers. They cannot be expressed by an ordinary row-level check alone.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Every account has at least one role and is at least 18 at registration (BR1, BR6).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;A volunteer has at most three preferred postal codes (BR9).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;A request has one to three active, valid pickup windows and an initial status-change entry (BR16, BR32).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Terms acceptances use the current document, correct actor and action type (BR29, BR38, BR43, BR54).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Delivery requires collection and a facility that accepts the request&amp;#x27;s category (BR25–BR28).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Award recipients match the assignment volunteer or request resident. Cancellation and self-delivery follow BR11 and contract section 15.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px&quot;&gt;Address edits, cancellation, collection, missed-pickup reports, expiry and deactivation follow their server transition rules (BR8, BR22, BR35, BR53).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="1400" height="2150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>